  "Rival Kazuo|Short selling blew my mind too. Think of it like this: you promise to deliver a card later, sell that promise for 12 Koins today, and when the card's price drops to 8, you grab one and deliver it. You keep the 4 Koin difference. Sneaky... but fair!": "5a17e39c01818396.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Step three: go to the small chart and wait for price to do something new right at the level \u2014 a candle that closes past the last little high or low. Then, and only then, you enter on the close . Big chart. 15-minute. Small chart. In that order, every time.": "0a34a3ae9d4d73da.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|The best ones do two things. A money hammer first dips under the low of the candle before it , then climbs back and closes green . A money shooter pokes over the last candle's high , then falls and closes red . It took a step one way and got turned right around.": "b10afe79ff31ad7c.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|The engulfing candle is my favourite \u2014 it is also called an outside bar . It takes out both sides of the candle before it: first it dips under that candle's low, then it climbs over its high. Whichever side it took out last is the way to expect price to keep going.": "7033ec683eff0e10.mp3",
