  "Rival Kazuo|This is your graduation battle. Everything you've learned, all at once. Ride the waves, wear your shield, keep your mind calm even when the dragon roars. I'll be watching, rival. Don't lose.": "297fb0f047387fba.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Three places matter in every trade. Your entry is where you get in. Your stop is where you get out if you are wrong. Your target is where you get out if you are right. Know all three before you click.": "255eddb7b3d62321.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|What decides the colour? Only two prices: where the candle opened and where it closed . Closed higher than it opened \u2014 green. Closed lower \u2014 red. The candle before it has nothing to do with it.": "fe7299e1c9b414fb.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|When price reaches a goal, Dad watches bodies first, wicks second . Price needs a candle body (close) beyond the level to keep going. If it only pokes its nose (wick) past and fails to close, it will bounce back!": "3abe7a6323e8c7ed.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Which line do you draw? Look to the left and count the touches. The line price bounced off the most times tells the best story \u2014 draw that one. And judge it by where candles closed , not where they poked.": "1a743fe4895e2286.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Why do these matter so much? Because crowds of traders park their orders \u2014 and their stops \u2014 right around them. Lots of orders in one spot is called liquidity . Price gets pulled toward it like a magnet.": "b43f1912cb3703e2.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Why so picky? Because breaking a fresh swing point proves strong buyers or sellers were really there. A gap that broke nothing new proved nothing. When price comes back to that one, do not expect it to hold.": "240bfb611919e4eb.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Why? Because the market loves to sweep (poke past) one side of these session candle ranges to trap eager retail traders in a trapdoor. Once the shields (stop orders) are gobbled up... SNAP, price reverses! That's a liquidity sweep .": "1a6cade6e4136ce1.mp3",
  "Rival Kazuo|Your stop-loss goes just beyond the zone. If a candle closes past it , your idea is INVALID \u2014 cut the trade instantly! No hoping, no moving stops. Give the trade max 2\u00bd hours to win; after that, let it go. Protect your Koins!": "f4a4e09911033b3b.mp3",
  "Sensei Hoshi|A candle has a thick body and thin wicks on top and bottom. The body shows where the price opened and where it closed .": "b7fd8d3adbebef06.mp3",
  "Sensei Hoshi|A chart with no lines is a map with no roads. Before the day begins, a trader draws a few key levels \u2014 the prices where something is most likely to happen.": "bccf98feb0153cd5.mp3",
  "Sensei Hoshi|A market is simply a place where people buy and sell things. A school card-trading club is a market! Some kids want to buy a rare card, some want to sell one.": "f6d924318730901a.mp3",
  "Sensei Hoshi|A strategy is a set of rules decided BEFORE the battle: when to enter, where the shield goes, when to leave. Rules protect you from your own excited heart.": "0e299871019e6ee0.mp3",
