  "|A red candle closed below where it opened: sellers won that one.": "9f18828b38e7a70c.mp3",
  "|A resting market stays about level. This one finished well above where it started.": "4ffeb274767491d9.mp3",
  "|A run of higher highs and higher lows is an uptrend . Buyers extend each push and give back less on each pullback. Candle colour is irrelevant here: a red candle that makes a new high is still a new high.": "f8fb097680900a29.mp3",
  "|A sliding market, so you sell first and the fall pays you. Both directions are tradable.": "4e6d8ecfd74f07ae.mp3",
  "|A small body on top with a long wick below is a hammer. The sellers attacked and lost.": "bc0ce7563970b483.mp3",
  "|A small fraction. At that size, a run of losing trades is a setback you can recover from, not the end of your account.": "f4bb17e089724d1c.mp3",
  "|A small slice! Then a losing streak is just a training montage, not game over.": "d3893570890f0b7b.mp3",
  "|A smaller balance: 50 Koins . What is 10% ?": "244b0e44b46f1e7d.mp3",
  "|A stop at entry is taken out by normal noise before the trade can work.": "7467e16b46e2df4e.mp3",
  "|A stop at your entry gets hit by a normal wiggle. You'd be out before the move even starts.": "a41e23ef9f3d7181.mp3",
  "|A strategy does not win every trade. It works over many trades by giving you an edge and keeping impulse out of your decisions. Take the quiz, then trade the breakout in the practice arena.": "71be1959cf1a140c.mp3",
  "|A strategy is a set of rules fixed before you trade: when to enter, where the stop-loss goes, when to exit. Rules protect you from decisions made in the heat of the moment.": "25baba9b4035b9eb.mp3",
  "|A strategy wins 3 trades in a row. What does that prove?": "3772f8989f603b8e.mp3",
  "|A strong ceiling (resistance) finally breaks. What does it often become?": "70de57aae0167bce.mp3",
  "|A swing high that is HIGHER than the last swing high is a\u2026": "bd9b8afa17e32d7b.mp3",
  "|A tie would wobble up and down. This one only goes one way.": "3b571e2a23a5de45.mp3",
  "|A timeframe is the amount of time one candle covers. A 1-hour chart shows the larger direction; a 2-minute chart shows the detail inside it. We call these higher and lower timeframes \u2014 HTF and LTF.": "c76b95354aa7ae37.mp3",
  "|A trade gets roughly two and a half hours. Past that, close it and wait for a new setup.": "5c023a3484e9f5aa.mp3",
  "|A trade has been open for three hours and never reached its target. What now?": "e710ec155e0ddd2b.mp3",
  "|A trade has been open three hours without reaching its target. What now?": "6b3c5633980615f3.mp3",
  "|A trader is certain a trade will win, so he skips his stop-loss. What difference does his certainty make to the market?": "80686cfdc1097833.mp3",
  "|A trader's protection is one decision made early : how many Koins am I willing to lose on this one trade?": "b61597809a8c3550.mp3",
  "|A trend is not an opinion. It is a sequence of swing points you can count, using four labels: HH, HL, LH, LL .": "23ea5a107bf9f74b.mp3",
  "|A turn is read in two steps. In a downtrend, the first higher high is the signal . Price then pulls back; if the pullback fails to take out the prior low, that higher low is the confirmation . The entry comes after the retrace, not on the first push. Reverse it for an uptrend: lower low is the signal, lower high is the confirmation.": "c6bfa4dd8a242e21.mp3",
  "|A typical example is a video claiming 'My trading bot made 2,000 in thirty minutes.' It is exciting, and it is tempting to pay the stranger for the secret. Watch such a video a second time, carefully, before doing anything.": "cabc66284e01dad6.mp3",
  "|A video claims: \"My bot made 2,000 in 30 minutes!\" What is the first question to ask?": "63f0a69ed0f1a2c9.mp3",
  "|A video says: 'My bot made 2,000 gold in 30 minutes!' What's the FIRST question a wise trader asks?": "41faea6fb2f13b55.mp3",
  "|A wick is only a test. A body closing beyond the last higher low is the break.": "30d10627adc18aa6.mp3",
  "|A wick is only a test. It takes a BODY closing below to break the staircase.": "f0b1852ad5805409.mp3",
  "|A wick poked under the last higher low, but the candle closed back above. Is the uptrend broken?": "53944034def34e7d.mp3",
  "|A zone that did not prove itself by doing something new will not hold; price goes straight through it. Do not trade off weak zones.": "591baa9a3e743472.mp3",
  "|A \u2014 Alignment (the timeframes). Your charts must agree. The 2-minute chart may look ready, but if the 15-minute and 1-hour charts say no, you are not aligned. Only trade in the direction of the higher timeframe.": "2f0ea7fa263394c1.mp3",
  "|About two and a half hours is the limit. After that, close it and wait for a fresh setup.": "cb8cf264deebd8cb.mp3",
  "|Above all of these: no exceptions . A rule that is bent once is no longer a rule. If you cannot follow it today, you are done for today.": "1c9bc4984cfecd7b.mp3",
  "|Above the middle of yesterday, buyers have the upper hand. Below it, sellers do.": "871777433ebed0b8.mp3",
  "|Above the midpoint of yesterday, buyers are in the stronger position.": "910393f214793fe4.mp3",
  "|Add the midpoint of yesterday's range \u2014 PD 50% , the equilibrium . Above it, buyers have the upper hand; below it, sellers do. That makes five lines you can draw before the day begins .": "ee084a09c3d1d941.mp3",
  "|Adding size increases risk beyond what the stop was sized for.": "4eddbc2a513e1ac5.mp3",
  "|After some losses you have 250 Koins . What is 2% of 250?": "ec61c3fd9bb157e8.mp3",
  "|After this course, what is true about real futures trading?": "725310bc25609676.mp3",
