  "|Compare the most recent hourly closes with those a few hours earlier: the direction is sideways.": "51a27c7e524e62e8.mp3",
  "|Complete the saying: \"The trend is your...\"": "b624b69d5e3c914b.mp3",
  "|Contracts multiply every point, in both directions. They never make a trade more likely to work.": "6d83273e896743bd.mp3",
  "|Correct!": "ba8cc7528587471f.mp3",
  "|Correct. Beyond the wick is where the idea is invalid \u2014 the chart sets the stop.": "1fe241413cf82a0d.mp3",
  "|Correct. Reaching a level is not an entry; a closed reaction candle is.": "32e4751e65e35089.mp3",
  "|Correct. The plan was set before entry; the job now is to leave it alone.": "52407df83288e976.mp3",
  "|Correct: down. Everything that follows is judged against that.": "603abf3b010c0772.mp3",
  "|Correct: sideways. Everything that follows is judged against that.": "4ea71940da36b04f.mp3",
  "|Count the steps. The hill marked \u201c?\u201d is a\u2026": "66a8945713aee211.mp3",
  "|D \u2014 Discipline (the rules). The strategy is worthless without your self-control: manage your emotions, stay patient, stay calm. The rules are max 3 trades a session , no alert = no trade , and no inside days. Follow the flowchart every time.": "a1e04c60c0258e76.mp3",
  "|DEMs and BIMs act like support and resistance. To find one in an uptrend, mark from the high of candle 1's wick to the low of candle 3's wick; in a downtrend, from the low of candle 1 to the high of candle 3. The empty space between is the gap.": "4ee2083ac494625c.mp3",
  "|DEMs and BIMs are simply the method's names for a fair value gap. They act like support and resistance and tend to attract price.": "9fa339342e2524a7.mp3",
  "|DEMs and BIMs! They are just Dad's nicknames for a fair value gap. They act like support and resistance and pull price like magnets.": "edf7d09040e4da3d.mp3",
  "|Dad watches the 50% and 75% marks \u2014 price dips there, holds, and continues. Much deeper can mean the zone is leaking!": "b20e17813b8055c9.mp3",
  "|Different day. What's this market doing \u2014 and which way do you go?": "a01c89c18ff4764b.mp3",
  "|Discipline is the skill that matters. Following the plan is the success; profits follow over time.": "c0094e920e738b75.mp3",
  "|Discipline is the superpower. Following the plan is the win \u2014 profits follow over time.": "ba1075d061e4d4a0.mp3",
  "|Do not mark everything. A cluttered chart causes hesitation. Mark only levels with a story \u2014 where control clearly changed hands \u2014 and never keep two redundant adjacent levels.": "15b1db9173fcb7d6.mp3",
  "|Don't take my word for it. Play the same game twice \u2014 once without the shield, once with it. Only the size of the LOSS changes. Watch.": "7e32f43283914ac8.mp3",
  "|Down Go Frazier! If a zone didn't prove itself by doing something new, price knocks it out immediately. Don't trade off weak zones!": "90125f2f77f7b468.mp3",
  "|Down the whole way. Sellers controlled the day.": "e0097657b01ecf53.mp3",
  "|Down the whole way. Sellers ran the day.": "e866875fb9e862bc.mp3",
  "|Down. That's the whole point: there are two ways to win , one for each direction.": "185ef36e4776a6d1.mp3",
  "|Downtrend \u2192 SHORT rides the wave down. LONG would be swimming against the current!": "373f13fe025a977e.mp3",
  "|Drop a ball on concrete and it bounces off the floor . Prices do that too \u2014 and the floor is usually a price they've bounced off before.": "203ac2a7a9726ebf.mp3",
  "|E \u2014 Execution (the setups). Trade only the method's two setups, the BNRs : (1) Bounce & Reject , the preferred one, at the outer highs and lows of a range, never the middle; (2) Break & Retest . Trade the second move , not the first \u2014 the method counts on price coming back to you.": "d5e456c763b7dad2.mp3",
  "|Each point has a dollar value. On the full-size NQ contract one point is $20 . On MNQ , the Micro, one point is $2 . The chart is identical; the Micro is one tenth the size.": "5bf854615b20107a.mp3",
  "|Easy money promises are the demon's favorite perfume. Real trading is slow, careful work.": "4268b09efdfac02d.mp3",
  "|Ended higher than it started \u2014 a GREEN candle. The thick body is start-to-end; the thin wicks are how far it stretched.": "af2317cbf4299b8e.mp3",
  "|Ended lower than it started \u2014 a RED candle. Sellers won that battle.": "11ba5148132fa397.mp3",
  "|Entries AT levels, targets FROM levels. Never the empty middle.": "37ecae32f2a443e4.mp3",
  "|Entries at the lines, targets from the lines. Never the empty middle.": "3adb06e53ca129fc.mp3",
  "|Entries at the lines, targets from the lines. The middle is where beginners get chopped up.": "9c711574d6ecc07c.mp3",
  "|Even a perfect plan loses sometimes. That's what 'edge' means \u2014 it wins OVER TIME, not every time.": "ef631271217e3808.mp3",
  "|Even a sound plan loses sometimes. That is what an edge means \u2014 it wins over time, not every time.": "9372bc9b3a6391b1.mp3",
  "|Even highly successful traders...": "a4ddcfc73b9f7e74.mp3",
  "|Even legendary traders...": "7128673bcb919bf7.mp3",
  "|Every candle is a fight. Buyers on the left. Sellers on the right. The bell rings, and price starts right here. That is the open.": "ac037907096465b7.mp3",
