  "|Fun, but no. Nothing on a chart has weight.": "94f6da998db1a5fe.mp3",
  "|Futures let you profit in either direction. Going long means you buy first, expecting the price to rise. Going short means you sell first, expecting it to fall, then buy back at a lower price. Both are routine in futures.": "2cc8a04e3feae8c3.mp3",
  "|Gaps are not equal. A higher-timeframe gap is the stronger one : a 1-hour gap outranks a 15-minute gap. When the higher and lower timeframes each have a gap in the same direction, that is the higher-probability setup.": "676dc3f5387c9f60.mp3",
  "|Going SHORT means you profit when...": "1c37d5df714a32c4.mp3",
  "|Going long means buying first, to profit if price rises. Going short means selling first, to profit if price falls. In futures both are routine.": "72c02b29d4cfe5eb.mp3",
  "|Going short means you profit when...": "5c36fc9a0aade44e.mp3",
